# Run 2026-10-31, worldgen block W1: earth fill (SQ-EF), on the recipe of structures/12_earth_fill_camps.md 2:
# group B, seed 8675309, srv toml [worldgen.debug] structureDensity = 4.0, [worldgen.earth_fill] log = "ALL",
# [worldgen.meta_structures] log = true. Three fresh worlds, rows chosen with --rows (plan steps W1a, W1b, W1c):
#   W1a  overrides = ["minecraft:village_plains=-1,-1", "village_savanna=-1,-1,-1"]  rows SQ-EF-01
#   W1b  no overrides (instance value)                                              rows SQ-EF-02 .. SQ-EF-11
#   W1c  W1b + beardFootprint = true                                                row SQ-TER-05
# Fill lines: [earth-fill]. A Chunky r 400 square takes about 4 min (2,500 chunks). The bot "qa" is only needed
# for rows that look at a place (spectator tp); console commands do the rest.
pace 2

## SQ-EF-01 | -1,-1 keeps the size's mound limit; -1,-1,-1 never prunes (W1a)
> chunky world minecraft:overworld
> chunky center 2144 -2592
> chunky radius 400
> chunky start
waitlog Task finished 1800
> execute positioned 0 70 0 run locate biome minecraft:savanna
waitlog nearest minecraft:savanna is at 300
capture SV is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> chunky center {SV1} {SV3}
> chunky radius 200
> chunky start
waitlog Task finished 1800
expect \[earth-fill\].*village_plains.*mound columns \(limit \d+\)
reject \[earth-fill\].*village_plains.*mound columns \(limit -1\)
reject \[earth-fill\].*village_savanna.*pruned
reject \[earth-fill\].*village_savanna.*CANCELLED
look savanna village lines show limit -1 and "-> kept" (ST-242); none in the savanna square = Chunky one more savanna square

## SQ-EF-02 | villages at a lake lose the wet houses only (W1b)
> chunky world minecraft:overworld
> chunky center 2144 -2592
> chunky radius 400
> chunky start
waitlog Task finished 1800
expect \[earth-fill\].*pruned \d+ of \d+ pieces.*footprint \d+ water / \d+ ground
look tp a spectator (pbot spawn qa X 150 Z minecraft:overworld creative, or the client block) to one pruned village: the dry part stands, no house over the lake (ST-239); W >= 16 in the reason; none: Chunky a coast square r 200 at -80 -16 and grep again

## SQ-EF-11 | small water never counts, predicted lines, census rejects (same world)
> celocate census 96 2144 -2592
waitlog (?i)census.*(done|finished|written) 2400
bootexpect \[earth-fill\].*too wet
bootexpect \[earth-fill\].*under 9 water.*-> kept
bootexpect \[earth-fill\].*\(predicted\)
bootreject \[earth-fill\].*under 9 water.*CANCELLED
look every "too wet" line has water >= 9 (python over RES/rows/SQ-EF-02.log + this one); census shows EARTH_FILL and PRIORITY rejects (ST-299)

